Now I have a complete picture. Let me compile my full analysis and design plan.

---

## Decoupling Plan: Runner Module from UI Implementation Details

### Problem Summary

The `run_with_ui()` method in `/private/var/folders/_q/qzh8_t6s15388qqf3p6n3d200000gp/T/bench-f0fdm451/src/runner/workflow.rs` has three coupling violations:

1. **Line 20, 317**: `use crate::ui::theme::BivvyTheme` / `let theme = BivvyTheme::new()` -- The runner directly constructs and uses `BivvyTheme` for formatting step headers, skip messages, and blocked status.

2. **Line 19, 602-616**: `use crate::ui::spinner::live_output_callback` -- The runner imports an `indicatif`-specific function and manually assembles the live output callback from a `ProgressBar`.

3. **Line 195 in mod.rs, line 603 in workflow.rs**: `SpinnerHandle::progress_bar()` returns `Option<ProgressBar>`, leaking `indicatif` into the trait contract. The runner calls `spinner.progress_bar()` to create the callback.

### Inventory of All Theme Usages in workflow.rs

From the grep results, the runner uses `theme` in these distinct patterns:

| Lines | What it formats | Pattern |
|-------|----------------|---------|
| 323, 329-334 | Skipped step messages (from `--skip` flag and environment filtering) | `theme.format_skipped(...)` |
| 359-374 | Step header: `[1/7] name` or `[1/7] name -- title` | `theme.step_number`, `theme.step_title`, `theme.dim` |
| 381 | Blocked status message | `StatusKind::Blocked.format(&theme, ...)` |
| 404 | Skipped (requirement not met) | `StatusKind::Skipped.format(&theme, ...)` |
| 453, 474 | Skipped (completed check) | `theme.format_skipped(...)` |
| 505 | Skipped (user declined in interactive) | `theme.format_skipped(...)` |
| 545 | Skipped (declined sensitive step) | `theme.format_skipped(...)` |

### Design: New Trait Methods

The key insight is that all runner theme usage falls into exactly three categories of presentation concern:

**A. Format a step header line** (the `[1/7] step_name -- title` line)
**B. Format a status message** (skip, blocked -- always indented with `"    "`)
**C. Create a live output callback** (from a spinner, without leaking ProgressBar)

#### New `UserInterface` methods

```rust
/// Format a step header line: "[index/total] name" or "[index/total] name -- title".
///
/// The runner calls this to get a formatted string it can display or embed
/// in prompts. Implementations handle styling (bold, dim, etc).
fn format_step_header(&self, name: &str, title: &str, index: usize, total: usize) -> String {
    // Default: plain formatting for backward compat
    let step_number = format!("[{}/{}]", index + 1, total);
    if name == title {
        format!("{} {}", step_number, name)
    } else {
        format!("{} {} -- {}", step_number, name, title)
    }
}

/// Format a status line (e.g., skip, blocked).
///
/// The runner calls this to produce styled status messages.
/// `kind` indicates the status type; implementations style accordingly.
